prompt_template:
Create one finished full-bleed raster editorial campaign poster. Visual family: Cream Curve Editorial, real hard-sun photography interwoven with huge flat warm-cream extra-condensed elastic typography.

Priority visual rules:
{STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}

Exact headline, once, no other text: "{MAIN_TEXT}".
Photographic content: {SUBJECT_SCENE}
Palette: {PALETTE}
Design intention: {DESIGN_DIRECTION}
Choose only the plan matching the requested canvas. 9:16 plan: {PORTRAIT_PLAN} 16:9 plan: {LANDSCAPE_PLAN}

Use hard natural sunlight and authentic small-scale surface detail, with fine low-strength photographic grain confined to photo regions. Cream lettering has clean smooth edges, flat fill, no extrusion, outline or drop shadow. Optical softness may occur naturally in the photograph. Do not add paper distress. Keep the headline legible and protect the crucial action at crossings. The result must look like a boldly art-directed photographic poster, with typography actually shaped by this subject. Sparse visual hierarchy; do not add a grid, border, secondary copy or logos.

Replace all source content: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}

Avoid malformed anatomy, duplicated objects, incoherent equipment, unreadable letters, misspellings, unmotivated ribbons, generic straight headline layouts, flat cartoon rendering, CGI skin, collage stickers, halftone, faux-vintage scratches, watermarks and creator marks.
